l 2026 was released for limited consultation only, including broadcasters and sporting codes with no public consultation process open to the millions of Australians who are directly affected by gambling harm and with the consultation period too brief to allow meaningful scrutiny; and (c) open letters from the crossbench as well as the Liberal Party, including from former Prime Minister the Hon John Howard OM AC and former Premier of Victoria the Hon Jeff Kennett AC, have recognised that the Government's proposed reforms to regulation of gambling do not go far enough; (2) recognises the importance of transparent consultation on significant legislative reforms; and (3) calls on the Government to undertake public consultation so that Australians affected by the legislation can engage with genuine co-design on the bill before its introduction. Leave not granted. I move: That so much of standing and sessional orders be suspended as would prevent the member for Kooyong from moving the following motion: That this House: (1) notes that: (a) gambling advertising causes significant health and financial harm to more than 3 million Australians every year; (b) the Government's exposure draft of the Interactive Gambling Amendment (Gambling Reform) Bill 2026 was released for limited consultation only, including broadcasters and sporting codes with no public consultation process open to the millions of Australians who are directly affected by gambling harm and with the consultation period too brief to allow meaningful scrutiny; and (c) open letters from the crossbench as well as the Liberal Party, including from former Prime Minister the Hon John Howard OM AC and former Premier of Victo","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-10268","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2026-06-22/1"}
